roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.05737025523686379,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":62.9,"_gate_rev_durability":0.20831500638537537,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.026429276043082244,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":40.5,"_gate_share_shrink":0.08296226455735578,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.018722579328639934,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":68.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.08745,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":58.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Nicolet Bankshares, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Nicolet National Bank that provides banking products and services for businesses and individuals in Wisconsin, Michigan, and Minnesota. The company accepts demand deposits, checking, savings, and money market accounts; various certificates of deposit; and individual retirement accounts. It also offers commercial loans, including commercial, industrial, and business loans and lines of credit; commercial real estate loans; agricultural (AG) production and AG real estate loans; commercial real estate investment loans; construction and land development loans; residential real estate loans, such as residential first lien and junior lien mortgages, home equity loans, and residential construction loans; and consumer loans. In addition, the company provides cash management, international banking, personal brokerage, safe deposit boxes, and trust and fiduciary services, as well as wealth management and retirement plan services. Further, it offers mortgage refinancing; online services, such as commercial, retail, and trust online banking; automated bill payment, mobile banking deposits and account access, and remote deposit capture services; and other services consisting of wire transfers, debit cards, credit cards, pre-paid gift cards, direct deposits, and official bank checks, as well as facilitates crop insurance products. The company was formerly known as Green Bay Financial Corporation and changed its name to Nicolet Bankshares, Inc. in March 2002. The company was incorporated in 2000 and is headquartered in Green Bay, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael E. Daniels | Co-Founder, President, CEO, Chairman & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $265K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 17%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $101K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Nicolet Bankshares Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.6B market cap on $392M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +21% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $149M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 38 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.02\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 8.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.25625641857196985},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 19% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Nickel Industries' (ASX:NIC) ENC Ramp-Up on Track?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/metal-and-mining/is-nickel-industries-asxnic-enc-ramp-up-on-track","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793941080.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ASX 200 mining stocks: Where does Nickel Industries (ASX:NIC) turn after its slide? - Kalkine Media","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/metal-and-mining/asx-200-mining-stocks-where-does-nickel-industries-asxnic-turn-after-its-slide","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793854620.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nicolet Bankshares Inc. (NIC) \u2013 What Are Brokerages Saying About This Stock?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/nicolet-bankshares-inc-nic-what-are-brokerages-saying-about-this-stock.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793788380.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Licence Key: What Will Unlock Nickel Industries' (ASX:NIC) ENC Sales?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/metal-and-mining/licence-key-what-will-unlock-nickel-industries-asxnic-enc-sales","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793767020.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nicolet Bankshares (NIC), What Is Behind The Fresh Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywa